}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 11670.25224018097, "notes": "ARC-063 crf-availability-maintenance substrate-readiness diagnostic (claim_ids=[], non_contributory -- does NOT weight governance). Supersedes V3-EXQ-666a. The readiness gate is RE-STATED on the ISOLATING statistic crf_frac_maintained (the maintained-reactivatable FRACTION = n_maintained / n_slots), NOT the gap-density-sensitive count floor crf_n_maintained_reactivatable >= 2 that 666a used (and that differentiation-alone cleared, the 666a measurement_test_design_defect). ARM_2 (maintenance) must clear crf_frac_maintained >= 0.625 where ARM_1 (mature+e2ctx, no maintenance) stays below 0.5 -- the discrimination the count floor could not deliver (666a ARM_2 1.0/0.625/0.938 vs ARM_1 0.188/0.125/0.438). A context-absent silence gap (CandidateRuleField.credit iterated GAP_TICKS times after behavioural-runtime training) sharpens ARM_1's erosion below the floor while activity-silent maintenance (maintenance_decay=0.0) HOLDS the ARM_2 pool -- robustifying the discrimination against gap density. Same-statistic non-vacuity discipline: minted>=2, full-pool differentiation, AND the ARM_2 maintained pool the fraction gate counts is itself a >=2-rule differentiated pool (count + differentiation readiness on the positive control); any unmet -> substrate_not_ready_requeue, never a false verdict. ARM_2 maintenance-ON is adopted as the mature-regime default. PASS clears the substrate_queue ready gate before the 654c GAP-B behavioural re-run (MECH-309 / ARC-062) is scored; that falsifier is the governance-weighting successor, queued separately. crf_frac_active ~0.016-0.031 in both e2ctx arms is the averaged-activity artefact the lit verdict identified -- kept as a secondary readout, NOT the persistence criterion. MECH-309/ARC-062/ARC-063 stay candidate / substrate_ceiling / v3_pending / pending_retest_after_substrate.", "queue_id": "V3-EXQ-666b", "machine": "ree-cloud-3"}